C3 -- REAL-NOISE CALIBRATION: what Delta chi^2 (kepler - framework) each TRUTH produces
==============================================================================================================
   Kepler truth    : Delta chi2 = +5.46 +/- 6.21  (N = 16)
   framework truth : Delta chi2 = +1.14 +/- 9.99  (N = 16)
   observed        : Delta chi2 = +3.79   (z = -0.27 under Kepler, +0.27 under framework; LR = 1.61)
  [PASS] C3 NO POWER: the observed value sits inside both truths (|z| < 1.5) and the framework-truth distribution is centred within 1 sd of zero
         measured: z_K = -0.27, z_F = +0.27, framework-truth mean/sd = +0.11, likelihood ratio 1.61
         reading:  UNDECIDABLE: the public cube cannot tell the framework from Kepler inside ~0.16" -- a null here is not evidence

==============================================================================================================
C4 -- THE KINEMATIC MASS IS PSF-SYSTEMATIC-LIMITED
==============================================================================================================
  [PASS] C4 log M (Kepler) moves by >= 0.5 dex between the PSF-free and PSF >= 0.16" fits
         measured: 6.67 -> 7.69 (+1.03 dex)
         reading:  the ~1 dex spread is exactly the 10^6.9-vs-10^7.7 gap that flips L324's sub-dominance verdict; the data favour a PSF sharper than JWST's ~0.17" diffraction limit at 5.28 um (a resampling artifact), so neither mass is secure

==============================================================================================================
E1-E3 -- THE EXTENDED GAS (0.1" bins, real-noise centroid errors)
==============================================================================================================
  [PASS] E1 the extended gas is blueshifted relative to the core
         measured: -12.1 +/- 5.2 km/s (-2.3 sigma)
         reading:  outflow-like (the paper also identifies an outflow at 300-450 pc)
  [PASS] E2 no rotation detected in the extended gas: dipole 95% upper limit (projected)
         measured: 8.4 km/s, 95% < 21.7 km/s
         reading:  the 300-450 pc rotation that would decide the law is NOT in the current data
  [PASS] E3 the extended gas is hot: if bound it needs >= 10x the black-hole mass
         measured: sigma = 74 (median) / 91 (flux-wtd) km/s; M_dyn(alpha=2) = 300 pc: 7.7e+08, 500 pc: 1.3e+09, 900 pc: 2.3e+09 Msun
         reading:  outflow (no test) OR bound: LCDM supplies a halo; the framework would need ~1e9 Msun of COLD GAS at 0.2-0.9 kpc (NOT sub-mm testable here: see E4) -- a registered conditional prediction

==============================================================================================================
E4 -- CAN SUB-MM DATA TEST THE BOUND-GAS CONDITIONAL?  ALMA 1.2 mm limit x the near-pristine metallicity
==============================================================================================================
  [PASS] E4 the ALMA dust limit cannot test ~1e9 Msun of cold gas in a near-pristine host
         measured: 3-sigma 0.1 mJy at 1.2 mm (Ma+25 citing Labbe+23/Fujimoto+23/Furtak+24), mu = 6.2, T_d = 25 K, CMB-corrected: M_dust < 1.5e+07 Msun; Z < 0.005 Zsun (Maiolino+25, arXiv:2505.22567) => GDR >= 2e+04 => M_gas < 3e+11 Msun
         reading:  the bound-gas branch is NOT sub-mm testable ([CII] fails for the same reason: almost no carbon) -- only kinematics can decide

==============================================================================================================
F1 -- THE CERTIFIED VELOCITY FLOOR (Lean I20)
==============================================================================================================
  [PASS] F1 v_flat = (G M a0)^{1/4} at 10^7.7: the floor below which no circular orbit may fall (isolated, no EFE)
         measured: canonical 28.1 km/s, alt 29.4 km/s
         reading:  a PSF-controlled rotation curve that falls below this beyond r_M ~ 250-270 pc falsifies the framework (Newton has no floor)

==============================================================================================================
VERDICT  (7/7 load-bearing PASS)
==============================================================================================================
  * THE TRUTH, as far as the public cube goes: UNDECIDABLE.  Kepler, the framework (both footings) and the a0 ~ H(z) rival
    fit the core equally well; real-noise injection shows the cube has NO power to separate them inside ~0.16"; the
    kinematic mass itself moves ~1 dex with the PSF assumption, so L324's mass-dependent sub-dominance verdict cannot
    be settled from these data either.
  * The extended gas is hot and blueshifted (outflow-like), with no detectable rotation: the decisive 300-450 pc
    rotation is not in the data.  IF it is bound, the framework needs ~1e9 Msun of cold gas there -- which the ALMA
    dust limit cannot test in this near-pristine (Z < 0.005 Zsun) host.
  * What would decide it: a PSF-controlled (source-plane) rotation curve beyond r_M ~ 250-270 pc, confronted with the
    certified floor v_c >= (G M a0)^{1/4} and the L324 K6 bands.
